<title>USA: U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Census Bureau reports factory consumption of domestic and foreign cotton (bales):</p>
<p>    Apr 97-A   Mar 97-B    Apr 96   Cum 1997   Cum 1996</p>
<p>     837,322  1,013,726   810,222  3,479,455  3,365,967</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE CONSUMPTION OF ALL COTTON (bales):</p>
<p>    Mar 97-Y   Feb 97-X   Mar 96</p>
<p>	40,486     38,989   39,506</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE SPINDLE HOURS OPERATED:</p>
<p>    Mar 97-X   Feb 96-Y   Mar 96</p>
<p>	   141	  139	146</p>
<p>A-4 weeks. B-5 weeks. X-Based on 00 days. Y-25 days.</p>
</text>
